{S}_U)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{example-presheaf}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-2-category-fibred-sets}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:81045f7978b9ffdb804598570a1b50fb3b73b795b13736f8cc86dcd82fbe24ff", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:dcd171ecd0f2d7ca172b718a2dc9c6798db4e8514c4776801d37db6cbef27ee0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d2a24abc7fde6afed465349161e7f14230c902cc61a98a0224aaf2f4759d6cac", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a category.\nThe only <MATH_0002>-morphisms between categories fibred in sets are identities.\nIn other words, the <MATH_0003>-category of categories fibred in sets is a category.\nMoreover, there is an equivalence of categories\n<MATHSEG_0001>the category of presheaves<MATHSEG_0002>of sets over <MATHSEG_0003>the category of categories<MATHSEG_0004>fibred in sets over <MATHSEG_0005>\nThe functor from left to right is the construction\n<MATH_0004> discussed in\nExample <REF_0001>.\nThe functor from right to left assigns to <MATH_0005>\nthe presheaf of objects <MATH_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:944b926f357872542889a1083d74c86ddf7b2cc65d5886e3ef7135c0ae338f62", "unit_id": "tag:02Y2:statement"}
